<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hurricane David</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1979</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hurricane <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> was a Category 5 Atlantic hurricane that struck Dominica on 29 August 1979 and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a> and the south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. On Dominica it destroyed most homes and the banana crop and left much of the population homeless. With more than 2,000 deaths in total, most in the Dominican Republic, it was one of the deadliest hurricanes of the century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hurricane-david.jpg" alt="Hurricane David" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:David_1979-08-31_1500Z.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
